From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonid <leonidy.1985@yandex.ru>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:36:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: bring the board description up to the full
 project series

The 7.3 port started from the 51-commit tree, which stopped before the
Wi-Fi, sensor, DVFS and USB work. Take the board DTS from the complete
77-patch series instead:

  - CONSYS/MT6631 and the Wi-Fi HIF node, both enabled, with the EMI
    reserve (0049, 0056)
  - MT6358 fuel gauge, invensense icm42607p IMU, sensortek stk3338 ALS/PS
    (0054, 0055, 0072)
  - CPU OPP tables for both clusters and the CPU thermal zone (0063, 0064)
  - GPU DVFS with the safe OPP subset (0059)
  - USB OTG: dr_mode = "otg", Type-C dual role with PD sink/source PDOs
    (0060, 0061, 0066, 0067)
  - HDMI output through the IT6112 bridge plus its two fixed regulators
    (0078)
  - SCP firmware reserve at 0x50000000, SCP and VDEC enabled (0080)

mt6771.dtsi therefore no longer deletes &scp/&vcodec_dec/&vcodec_enc; the
T800 board has no SCP reserve, so it deletes them itself.

Also repair a comment the series split in two: the CONSYS block had been
inserted between the opener of the "No own ramoops node on purpose"
comment and its body, which left a dangling comment fragment after the
node and made dtc fail with a syntax error.
