- * the rail stays disabled (regulator_summary: vcn33 use_count=0). With the rail
- * off those windows still *read* (chip id 0x788, LSR=0x60 come from a stale
- * path) but every write is dropped: IER/TRI_LVL/THR, the MCR doorbell
- * (0x1807xx) and APC_CON all read back unchanged. That is exactly the
- * "BTIF write-dead" wall from docs/STATUS.md 13.11 (4)-(7).
- *
- * The vendor kernel enables the rail from its WMT driver through the stock
- * "vcn33_bt"/"vcn33_wifi" handles. Keep it on: the cost is a few mA and it
- * makes the whole CONN register window writable.
- */
